    13	| **5. Get 35 of 44 right twice, with at least 28 written.** | This guards against a system that rarely produces usable questions. Its product importance comes from that missing coverage. The fixed count is achievable on this set under some readings. Astra’s recorded result was **40 right / 31 written** or **35 / 26**. Applying the existing due-day rule in a separate recount gave **40 / 31** or **39 / 30**. **Report it as a repeatability measure.** Use source-defined important matters, including those neither system opens, to decide product coverage. [D400](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4384) · [Recorded and counterfactual counts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/LOG.md:25) |
    14	| **6. Keep the favourable direction every time and the due day nine times in ten.** | **High impact if the direction is backwards or a question closes before evidence can settle it.** Exact agreement is measurable by code. Astra agreed on direction for **9/9** applicable topics and on dates for **32/33**. In the October reading, date agreement was **7/8** on the wider set, below 90%. **Keep code-owned dates and stored direction rules enforced. Report agreement across draws, and check whether the direction and deadline are correct on the product card.** A repeated date can still be wrong. [Astra counts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/codex-cold.md:25) · [October counts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/second-week/RESULT.md:61) · [Date rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/ladder_step.py:289) |
