    16	D623’s rates are descriptive, from overlapping luna-era readings. Under an independence assumption, a combined fault rate of about **0.53% per send** gives only a coin-flip chance of seeing zero faults in 131 sends. That calculation explains why a clean run is weak evidence of a repeatable pass. It does not estimate astra’s production fault rate. [D623 underlying counts and assumptions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/codex-cold.md:15)
    17	
    18	### 2. What should decide readiness
    19	
    20	**Use the July–August comparison to find product failures. Use a matched comparison against current production to decide release.** For the proposed D663 reading, use fresh new-system output for the weeks starting July 20 through August 24 and the old output available as of the same dates. The exposure check establishes that these articles are unread by new-system Step 1 in the recorded runs. The old archive ends August 28, so use the same partial final week on both sides. Also, the sealed archive came from `poc-v34`, while current production replay uses `poc-v118`. Label this result as a comparison with the archived product. D431 specifies current production and three same-day draws each for the formal comparison. [D663](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9374) · [Exposure correction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison-feasibility/RESULT.md:27) · [Archive and replay versions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:132) · [D431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4795)
    21	
    22	**Primary measure: the share of important matters for which the analyst gets a usable answer.** Have both reader families name those matters from the articles before seeing either system’s output. On each matter, a system earns one credit if it asks the right question, has a clear way and time to settle it, and shows an answer supported by the facts available at the cutoff. A duplicate earns no extra credit. A missed matter, missing answer or unresolved mark stays in the denominator. Report coverage and support separately as well. Otherwise a system could look better simply by skipping the hardest questions. [Source-first reading and denominators](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN.md:21) · [Product goal](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:22)
    23	
    24	I propose **10 percentage points as the material difference**, roughly one additional usable answer per ten important matters. Use a prewritten 95% interval for the new-minus-old difference, accounting for matters and weeks shared by both systems:
    25	
    26	- **Better:** the lower bound is above **+10 points**.
    27	- **No worse shown:** the lower bound is above **−10 points** and the better rule is unmet. This can include a possible improvement that remains unproven.
    28	- **Worse:** the upper bound is below **−10 points**.
    29	- **Unclear:** everything else. A missed control or a comparison that fails its input checks yields **no verdict**.
    30	
    31	These are proposed decision margins. The record leaves “beats” undefined and shows that earlier support differences even changed sign across weeks. Require **better** for the quality case to replace production. Also adopt the proposed checks on the new system’s own output: **at least 80%** of important matters covered, **at most 20%** trivial or duplicate questions, **at least 90%** of last answers supported, **at most 5%** of checked citations materially wrong, and **zero confirmed omissions that would change an answer in the audited facts**. Apply those floors in at least two of the three release draws. Report insufficient and unresolved answers separately and give them no credit toward 90%. The missing-fact check needs a known consequential example to show it can detect one. [Undefined comparison margin](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:126) · [Observed differences](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md:28) · [Proposed quality floors and controls](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN.md:33)
    32	
    33	**Minimum size.** Six full weeks would yield about **42 new and 90 old answer cards** before allowing for the partial week or repeat questions. Applying the existing sizing formula to those counts, even independent cards would reliably detect only a gap of about **22 points**. The record estimates **7–9 weeks** for a 20-point gap versus zero. For the proposed decision, a true gain of 20 must clear a margin of 10. The same simple formula gives an illustrative workload of **about 30 weeks, or 210 new and 450 old cards**, to resolve that 10-point separation with 80% power. This is a planning estimate for raw support, since the proposed paired measure has a different denominator. Set the actual minimum before reading outputs. Require at least **80% power** to distinguish a true gain or loss of 20 points from its 10-point boundary, and to establish no worse at a true tie. Size that calculation on distinct matters and paired weeks. Repeated cards about the same matter do not buy independent evidence. The six-week archive comparison is a diagnostic under this rule. [Sizing assumptions and observed counts](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md:37) · [Sizing formula](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/sizing.py:29)
    34	
    35	### 3. Gates 2 to 5
    36	
    37	| Gate | Recommendation |
    38	|---|---|
    39	| **2. Are the answers supported?** | **Fold the quality requirements into the product comparison.** Keep D428’s separate figure and event limits: unsupported figure answers at most **five points above the stated baseline**, unsupported event answers at most **5%**, and unsupported last decided answers at most **3 in 30**. Report insufficient answers and judgment coverage alongside them. Require enough examples of both types before treating those checks as exercised. The historical test remains unpassed with **4 of 8** comparable controls and a strict last-answer result of **3/24**. Its reference work, D658, waits. Record explicitly that the new product checks replace this test for future release decisions if the council adopts that change. [D428](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4756) · [Stage B result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/STAGE_B_RESULT.md:12) · [D664](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9390) |
    40	| **3. Does it beat current production?** | **Keep as a release requirement.** Use the product margin above for “beats.” Preserve the frozen-reference comparison and Step 2’s three checks under D427/D431. The proposed archive reading does not satisfy that commitment. [D427](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4738) · [D431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4795) |
    41	| **4. Can an analyst use it on unseen news?** | **Fold into the same release comparison.** Use the source-first matter list, output quality floors, and evidence audit on fresh material. D484 opened this work, and the numerical floors remain proposals until adopted. [D484](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:5488) · [Proposed floors](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/ACCEPTANCE-DESIGN.md:44) |
